<title>UK: BP, oil stocks off after negative comment.</title>
<headline>BP, oil stocks off after negative comment.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK oil stocks dropped on Wednesday after the influential Financial Times Lex column said oil prices could come under pressure during 1997, undermining share prices in the sector, traders said.</p>
<p>British Petroleum Co Plc was down 6-1/2p at 682 by 1300 GMT, Shell Transport &amp; Trading Co was down 1-1/2p at 993-1/2, Enterprise Oil Plc was down 8p at 579 and Lasmo Plc was down 2-1/2p at 216.</p>
<p>Lex said additional crude supply would come on stream next year and that the &quot;threat to oil shares from a more realistic environment next year is obvious.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 5106</p>
